---
description: graphify knowledge graph context
alwaysApply: true
---

Use Graphify only when `graphify-out/graph.json` exists.

When that file exists, run Graphify before exploring the codebase:

- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for any codebase or architecture question
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — all nodes related to a concept

This applies to every subagent that explores code. After modifying code files, run `graphify update .` (AST-only, no API cost).

When `graphify-out/graph.json` does not exist, Graphify is not installed for this project. Use ordinary file search and reads. Do not install Graphify or add a package script unless asked.
